{%- render 'section-design', section: section -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Six pairs of hands: the Kaarigar painting, six makers each in a painted
  arch. Over each panel lies a hover area; hovering it (focus, or a tap on a
  phone) plays that craft's film inside the panel's own window, cut to the
  arch's outline, in 1080p through snippets/sj-film-url. Each craft's name,
  mark and line sit under its panel. A village and a pot on its wall sit in
  the corners, moving at their own depths as the section passes.

  The panels and windows are traced from the painting
  (awwwards-preview/six_geometry.json), so the six crafts are fixed
  settings rather than blocks. Styles and behaviour are the home page
  layer's (assets/sj-home.css and sj-home.js, from awwwards-preview/src/
  six.css and six.js).

  Written by awwwards-preview/write_poster.py from six_shapes.py, which
  also draws the preview: change it there and run both scripts.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign art = s.art_asset | default: 'sj-karigar.webp' | asset_url
  if s.pot != blank
    assign corner_pot = s.pot | image_url: width: 1000
  else
    assign corner_pot = s.pot_asset | default: 'sj-six-pot.webp' | asset_url
  endif
-%}
